# VibeLaunch Platform Specification

## Overview

VibeLaunch is a full-stack platform for founders to launch products on X (Twitter) with AI-powered content generation, engagement analytics (ERI), vector-based learning, and SEO changelog publishing.

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with pgvector extension
- **ORM**: Prisma
- **Auth**: NextAuth.js with X OAuth 2.0
- **Queue**: Upstash QStash
- **AI**: OpenAI (embeddings + content generation)
- **Media**: Sharp
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS

## Phase 1: Foundation

### Prisma + pgvector
- Schema in `prisma/schema.prisma`
- pgvector extension enabled for `PostEmbedding.embedding` (vector 1536)
- Models: User, Account, Session, Project

### X OAuth
- NextAuth Twitter provider v2.0
- Scopes: `tweet.read tweet.write users.read offline.access`
- Stores `xUserId` and `xUsername` on User

### Project CRUD
- `GET/POST /api/projects` — list and create
- `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/projects/[id]` — read, update, delete
- Dashboard UI at `/dashboard`

## Phase 2: Publishing Pipeline

### Media Engine
- `src/lib/media/engine.ts` — Sharp-based image processing
- Validates URLs, resizes to X constraints (4096px, 5MB)

### QStash Post Queue
- `src/lib/queue/qstash.ts` — enqueue with delay/scheduling
- `POST /api/queue/process` — webhook handler with signature verification
- `POST /api/posts/[id]/publish` — enqueue a post

### X Publish
- `src/lib/x/publish.ts` — publish tweets + media upload
- Fetches engagement metrics via X API v2

## Phase 3: Analytics & AI

### ERI Analytics Cron
- `POST /api/cron/eri` — fetches metrics, creates EriSnapshots
- ERI formula: `(likes + retweets*2 + replies*1.5 + clicks*0.5) / impressions * 100`

### Vector Reinforcement
- `src/lib/vector/embeddings.ts` — OpenAI embeddings stored in pgvector
- High-ERI posts (≥2.0) get reinforced embeddings

### Adaptive Generator
- `POST /api/generate` — generates content inspired by top-performing posts
- `src/lib/generator/adaptive.ts` — uses vector similarity + OpenAI

## Phase 4: SEO

### SEO Expander
- `src/lib/seo/expander.ts` — expands summaries into full SEO content

### Changelog Pages
- `/changelog/[slug]` — public changelog entries with metadata

### Sitemap
- `/sitemap.xml` — dynamic XML sitemap of published changelogs

### Google Indexing
- `src/lib/seo/google-indexing.ts` — Indexing API via service account JWT

### SEO Publish API
- `POST /api/seo/publish` — create changelog, expand SEO, request indexing

## Phase 6: GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)

### Prisma
- `GeoMetric` model linked to `Project` — tracks citation checks per LLM provider and query prompt

### Citation Tracker
- `src/lib/geo/citation-tracker.ts` — `checkLLMCitations(projectId)` queries Perplexity, ChatGPT, and Claude
- `detectCitation()` parses responses for project name/domain mentions

### LLM Schema Engine
- `src/lib/geo/llm-schema.ts` — `SoftwareApplication`, `FAQPage`, and `Article` JSON-LD for changelog pages
- Injected on `/changelog/[slug]` via `buildGeoJsonLd()`

### GEO Dashboard
- `components/dashboard/geo-card.tsx` — citation score, AI engine badges, content tweak suggestions
- `GET /api/geo/metrics` — fetch citation analytics
- `POST /api/geo/check` — trigger fresh LLM citation scan

## Phase 7: Autonomous Verification & Diagnostic Agent

### Prisma
- `TestRun` model linked to `Project` — stores suite results, score, status, and assertion details (JSON)

### Diagnostic Suites
- `seo_audit` — changelog SEO metadata, Google indexing, JSON-LD schema readiness
- `feedback_loop` — vector reinforcement for high-ERI posts, embedding sync, ERI snapshots
- `media_render` — media URL validation, Sharp processing, code card render integrity
- `geo_audit` — GEO citation score, per-provider coverage, check freshness

### Agent & Cron
- `src/lib/diagnostics/agent.ts` — `runAllDiagnostics()`, `runDiagnosticSuite()`, `runDiagnosticsForAllProjects()`
- `POST /api/cron/diagnostics` — autonomous verification across all active projects
- `GET /api/diagnostics/runs` — fetch latest test run results
- `POST /api/diagnostics/run` — trigger manual diagnostic scan

### Dashboard
- `components/dashboard/diagnostic-card.tsx` — platform health score and per-suite status

## Environment Variables

See `.env.example` for all required variables.

## Testing

```bash
npm test          # vitest unit tests
npm run build     # production build
npx prisma generate
```

## Directory Structure

```
src/
  app/           # Next.js pages and API routes
  lib/
    analytics/   # ERI calculations and cron
    generator/   # Adaptive content generation
    media/       # Image processing
    queue/       # QStash integration
    seo/         # SEO expander, sitemap, Google indexing
    geo/         # GEO citation tracker, LLM schema, analytics
    diagnostics/ # Autonomous verification agent and audit suites
    vector/      # pgvector embeddings
    x/           # X/Twitter publish
prisma/          # Database schema
.memory-bank/    # Project context for agents
```
